Based on the codebase, here are the 4 Interview APIs with their theoretical explanations:

1. POST /api/v1/interviews - Create Interview & Generate Questions
Purpose: Creates a new interview for a specific candidate and job, then uses AI to generate relevant technical questions.

Theory:

Takes a job_id and candidate_id as input
Retrieves the job requirements (required/preferred skills) from the database
Retrieves the candidate's skills from their parsed resume
Passes this information to the Interview Agent (LLM)
The Interview Agent generates customized questions based on:
Job title and requirements
Candidate's skill gaps
Technical depth needed for the role
Questions are stored in the database with topics (e.g., "Database Optimization", "API Design")
Returns the interview ID and generated questions
Use Case: When a recruiter wants to start the interview process for a shortlisted candidate.

2. GET /api/v1/interviews/{id} - Get Interview Details
Purpose: Retrieves an existing interview with all its questions for review.

Theory:

Takes an interview_id as input
Fetches the interview record from the database
Eagerly loads all associated questions (prevents N+1 query problem)
Returns the interview status, job/candidate info, and all questions with their IDs
Useful for displaying the interview interface to the candidate or reviewer
Use Case: When a candidate needs to see their interview questions, or a recruiter wants to review the interview setup.

3. POST /api/v1/interviews/{id}/answers - Submit Candidate Answers
Purpose: Allows a candidate to submit their answers to the interview questions.

Theory:

Takes an interview_id and a dictionary of {question_id: answer_text}
Validates that all submitted question IDs belong to this interview
Stores each answer in the database linked to its question
Updates the interview status to answers_submitted
The answers are persisted for later evaluation
Use Case: When a candidate completes their interview and submits their responses.

4. POST /api/v1/interviews/{id}/evaluate - Evaluate Interview
Purpose: Uses AI to score the candidate's answers and provide detailed feedback.

Theory:

Takes an interview_id as input
Retrieves the interview with questions and answers (eagerly loaded)
Retrieves the job requirements for context
Passes the following to the Evaluation Agent (LLM):
Job title and required skills
Question-answer pairs
The Evaluation Agent scores each answer on:
Technical accuracy
Depth of understanding
Communication clarity
Provides an overall assessment with:
Technical Knowledge score (0-10)
Problem Solving score (0-10)
Communication score (0-10)
Role Fit score (0-10)
Overall score (0-10)
Written summary
Per-question feedback with scores
Stores the evaluation in the database
Updates interview status to evaluated
Use Case: After a candidate submits answers, the recruiter runs evaluation to get AI-powered scoring and detailed feedback.

Complete Interview Workflow:
1. Create Interview (POST /interviews)
   ↓
   Job + Candidate → Interview Agent → Questions Generated
   ↓
2. Get Interview (GET /interviews/{id})
   ↓
   Display questions to candidate
   ↓
3. Submit Answers (POST /interviews/{id}/answers)
   ↓
   Candidate answers → Stored in database
   ↓
4. Evaluate Interview (POST /interviews/{id}/evaluate)
   ↓
   Q&A Pairs + Job Context → Evaluation Agent → Scores & Feedback